{% comment %}
  Phase 1 debug markup — text only, deliberately.

  This renders every field the endpoint sends, as plain lines, so an
  end-to-end test has nothing to debug but the data: if a station is wrong,
  a walk time is ignored, or a card fails, it is visible here without CSS
  between you and it.

  The real UI is phase 2 and will be built on the TRMNL design framework
  (screen / view / layout / columns, with Item rows). See the spec's §3.2 —
  the framework measures content height at runtime, which changes how many
  rows a card should carry, so there is no point styling this first.

  Row tuples are [badge, destination, time, urgent].
{% endcomment %}

<div class="view">
  <div class="layout">
    <pre style="font-size:12px; line-height:1.35; white-space:pre-wrap;">
generated {{ t }}
cards: {{ c | size }}
{% for card in c %}
--------------------------------------------------
slot {{ card.s }}  {{ card.y }}  "{{ card.n }}"
{%- if card.b %}  bullets: {{ card.b | join: "," }}{% endif %}
{%- if card.e %}
  !! ERROR: {{ card.e }}
{%- else %}
{%- for col in card.k %}
  [{{ col.h | default: "(no heading)" }}]  {{ col.r | size }} rows
{%- for r in col.r %}
    {{ r[0] }} | {{ r[1] }} | {{ r[2] }}{% if r[3] == 1 %} *URGENT{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if col.r == empty %}
    (no upcoming departures)
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{% endfor %}
--------------------------------------------------
{% if c == empty %}
No cards configured. Set at least one card's transit type and station.
{% endif %}
    </pre>
  </div>

  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">NYC Transit</span>
    <span class="instance">debug build</span>
  </div>
</div>
